{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q018_tal_effector_repeat_lengths\",\"answer\":\"In SCOPe 2.08, all three domains have the same family lineage: all-alpha class a, left-handed alpha-alpha-superhelix fold a.298, TAL-effector-like superfamily a.298.1, and TAL effector family a.298.1.1. They are PthA (d2kq5a_), dHax3 (d3v6pa_), and BurrH (d4cj9a_), respectively. Their unequal lengths—51, 373, and 752 residues in the genetic SEQRES domain representations—reflect the defining biology of this repeat family: homologous approximately 34-residue TAL repeats occur in variable-copy tandem arrays, sometimes with flanking residues. SCOPe explicitly marks this as repeat-count heterogeneity; d2kq5a_ is annotated as a single repeat, whereas d3v6pa_ and d4cj9a_ contain progressively longer repeat arrays. Thus family membership concerns homology of the repeat module and conserved superhelical architecture, not equal total length or a one-to-one alignment across the full proteins. The family’s canonical representative repeat is d4cj9a_, chain A residues 259–292, but those coordinates apply only to d4cj9a_; they must not be transferred directly to d2kq5a_ or d3v6pa_, nor does this designation make d4cj9a_ the best full-length template for every array. A single-repeat structure can support local repeat modeling but cannot by itself specify a longer array’s repeat count, global curvature, interfaces, or termini. Likewise, family membership supports close evolutionary relatedness but does not justify transferring an exact DNA target, specificity, or complete biochemical function: those depend importantly on repeat number, order, and repeat-variable residues and require target-specific sequence/structural and functional evidence.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info\",\"/api/v1/releases/current\",\"mcp__scope__get_scop_domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/parents\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/annotations\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/homology\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/parents\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/annotations\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/homology\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/parents\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/annotations\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/homology\",\"mcp__scope__get_scop_sequence\",\"/api/v1/sequences/sids/d2kq5a_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json\",\"/api/v1/sequences/sids/d3v6pa_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json\",\"/api/v1/sequences/sids/d4cj9a_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json\"]}]}"}}
